# 🐱🐶 Cat vs Dog Image Classification using ResNet18

An end-to-end deep learning image classification project that uses **PyTorch** and **ResNet18 Transfer Learning** to classify images as either **Cat** or **Dog**.

This project was developed as part of a Deep Learning mini-project focused on building, training, evaluating, and documenting a complete deep learning pipeline.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

Image classification is one of the fundamental applications of deep learning.

In this project, a pretrained **ResNet18** convolutional neural network is used to classify images into two classes:

- 🐱 Cat
- 🐶 Dog

Instead of training a deep CNN completely from scratch, **transfer learning** is used. ResNet18 is first loaded with pretrained ImageNet weights, and its final classification layer is adapted for the two-class problem.

The project covers the complete workflow:

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Data Cleaning
   ↓
Train / Validation / Test Split
   ↓
Image Preprocessing
   ↓
Data Augmentation
   ↓
DataLoader
   ↓
Pretrained ResNet18
   ↓
Transfer Learning
   ↓
Training
   ↓
Validation
   ↓
Testing
   ↓
Evaluation
   ↓
New Image Prediction
